-# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-knowledge-scope
-
-English | [中文](README.zh.md)
-
-Chrome-extension-only composer control for selecting code repositories directly and, when needed, a knowledge domain and knowledge-base systems before a continuable Knowledge subagent searches them. A persistent scope row is the composer card's immediately preceding sibling, with separate repository and knowledge triggers; each opens its own upward panel. Repositories support multi-selection through a domain → system → repository tree when the extension catalog supplies the optional relations; otherwise they stay in an explicit ungrouped branch. It starts only in the nonce-bound loopback iframe, requests catalog and selection snapshots from the extension, and sends scope updates back over the same origin- and nonce-checked channel. The control does not fetch Knowledge Platform data, persist selection, add prompt text, or add model tool arguments.
-
-## Model Experience
-
-### Extension scope command
-
-#### What the model sees
-
-`knowledge-scope-command/v1` is a loopback UI message and never becomes prompt text, a model tool argument, or a session event.
-
-#### Token effect
-
-Zero direct token effect; the Connector adapter, not this UI package, supplies the selected scope to an executed search.
-
-#### KV Cache effect
-
-None; the package does not alter a provider request or a reusable prompt prefix.
-
-## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
-
-- **Extension-only availability** — ordinary Web sessions do not register the selector because they have no trusted Chrome-extension parent.
-- **Extension-owned data** — catalog availability, selection persistence, and authenticated Knowledge Platform requests depend on the companion Chrome extension.
